<title>CHINA: China bans imports of UK poultry on disease fears.</title>
<headline>China bans imports of UK poultry on disease fears.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has banned imports of British poultry and poultry-related products after several outbreaks of the Newcastle virus in the United Kingdom, the Xinhua news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ban came into effect from June 18 and any poultry or poultry-related products imported since then would have to be returned or destroyed, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>Since the beginning of this year there Britain has had 11 cases of Newcastle disease, an acute viral disease of poultry, four on chicken farms and seven on turkey farms, the agency said without giving further details. --Beijing Newsroom (86-10) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
